  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "For each function $f(x)$, find the inverse function $g(x)$ and state its domain.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=2x-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=\\dfrac{x+3}{2}$; domain: all real numbers.",
          "worked": "Write $y=2x-3$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=2y-3\\\\x+3&=2y\\\\y&=\\frac{x+3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThus $g(x)=\\dfrac{x+3}{2}$, with domain all real numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x-1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=2x+1$; domain: all real numbers.",
          "worked": "Write $y=\\dfrac{x-1}{2}$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{y-1}{2}\\\\2x&=y-1\\\\y&=2x+1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $g(x)=2x+1$, with domain all real numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=2^x-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=\\log_2(x+3)$; domain: $x>-3$.",
          "worked": "Write $y=2^x-3$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=2^y-3\\\\x+3&=2^y\\\\y&=\\log_2(x+3)\\end{align*}$$\nThe logarithm requires $x+3>0$. Thus $g(x)=\\log_2(x+3)$, with domain $x>-3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\log_3(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=3^x-1$; domain: all real numbers.",
          "worked": "Write $y=\\log_3(x+1)$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\log_3(y+1)\\\\3^x&=y+1\\\\y&=3^x-1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $g(x)=3^x-1$, with domain all real numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=8-x^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{8-x}$; domain: all real numbers.",
          "worked": "Write $y=8-x^3$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=8-y^3\\\\y^3&=8-x\\\\y&=\\sqrt[3]{8-x}\\end{align*}$$\nCube roots are defined for every real input. Thus $g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{8-x}$, with domain all real numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^3-8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x+8}$; domain: all real numbers.",
          "worked": "Write $y=x^3-8$ and interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=y^3-8\\\\x+8&=y^3\\\\y&=\\sqrt[3]{x+8}\\end{align*}$$\nCube roots are defined for every real input. Thus $g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x+8}$, with domain all real numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
